      "writtenOn": "2023-11-27T08:13:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e This should be moved to after the known-answer suppression check, otherwise this boolean would be incorrect.\n\nMake sense. Update the design accordingly.\n\n\u003e I first thought that it would be OK to include the SRV, TXT, address records in the additional section even if the PTR was known, but you\u0027d possibly end up in cases where there\u0027s no record in the answer section at all, and only records in the additional section, which doesn\u0027t seem valid.\n\u003e\n\u003e Would you be able to test what Android S (mdnsresponder) does when the PTR record is in the known answers ? I\u0027d expect that it sends no reply to PTR questions ?\n\nI have tested the DUPLICATE SUPPRESSION test case of BCT using an Android S phone. The mDnsResponder does not send a reply to PTR questions if the PTR record is present in the known answers. Our current implementation does not send a response in the absence of an answer, so it won\u0027t have an invalid response containing only records in the additional section. However, I believe the issue may arise when dealing with multiple questions where the PTR record is present in the known answers but other records remain in the additional section.",
      "parentUuid": "1228b4e1_677f9b29",
